│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the original per-layer Python packing loops with a batched   │
│                          │ capped-LPT scheduler. It processes all MoE layers simultaneously while preserving exact   │
│                          │ slot capacities: heavy groups or replicas are considered first and assigned to the        │
│                          │ currently least-loaded eligible destination.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The design keeps hierarchical locality when group-to-node partitioning is possible, but   │
│                          │ improves placement efficiency through vectorized tensor updates rather than nested Python │
│                          │ list/min operations. Replica creation uses batched marginal load reduction: each          │
│                          │ additional replica is assigned to the logical expert with the highest current per-replica │
│                          │ pressure. The resulting replicas are then packed across GPUs with the same capacity-aware │
│                          │ scheduler, improving GPU balance without violating per-GPU physical-expert counts.        │
