│ patch_description        │ Replace the Python-level per-layer/per-expert packing loop with a batched tensor          │
│                          │ implementation of the same capacity-constrained LPT greedy policy.                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The previous implementation repeatedly converts tensor values into Python operations      │
│                          │ while selecting a pack for every group. This creates substantial interpreter overhead,    │
│                          │ particularly when there are many MoE layers, groups, or repeated balancing calls. The     │
│                          │ replacement processes all layers simultaneously for each sorted group position: it        │
│                          │ chooses the least-loaded non-full pack per layer, writes the selected pack/rank with      │
│                          │ scatter operations, and updates pack loads/counts with scatter_add.                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves the important balancing behavior: groups are processed in descending load  │
│                          │ order and each is assigned to the currently lightest eligible pack, while every pack      │
│                          │ receives exactly the required number of groups. It also avoids forced CPU index           │
│                          │ transfers, allowing the helper to remain efficient if called with tensors already on an   │
│                          │ accelerator.                                                                              │
