│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_refine_packing                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded batched exchange-refinement phase after LPT packing. LPT is fast but can    │
│                          │ leave avoidable imbalance because its greedy assignments are never reconsidered. The      │
│                          │ refinement examines exchanges between items in the currently heaviest pack and items in   │
│                          │ other packs, selecting the exchange that reduces the row's maximum pack load. It          │
│                          │ preserves the exact per-pack capacity constraint by swapping items and their assigned     │
│                          │ slots.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search is limited to small packing problems, where the quadratic candidate matrix is  │
│                          │ inexpensive and where GPU-local packing most commonly operates. This improves GPU load    │
│                          │ balance without imposing significant planning overhead for large group-level packing      │
│                          │ problems.                                                                                 │
