│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_refined_packing                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Add a bounded best-improving pair-swap refinement after the batched                       │
│                          │ cardinality-constrained LPT placement.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ LPT is fast and usually produces good placements, but it can leave two packs with         │
│                          │ complementary mistakes: a relatively heavy item in a heavily loaded pack and a lighter    │
│                          │ item in a lightly loaded pack. Swapping those items preserves the exact per-pack item     │
│                          │ quota while reducing the sum of squared pack loads, which directly reduces residual       │
│                          │ GPU/node imbalance.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The refinement evaluates all cross-pack item pairs in parallel and applies at most two    │
│                          │ best swaps per layer. It is intentionally restricted to moderately sized packing problems │
│                          │ so that the quadratic candidate matrix cannot dominate planner runtime for unusually      │
│                          │ large expert configurations. The main EPLB packing stages normally operate on groups or   │
│                          │ physical experts per node, where this inexpensive local search has high value.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0392                                                                                   │
