│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lexicographic_swap_refinement                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ Improve the GPU/node packing local-search phase with a lexicographic objective. The       │
│                          │ current refinement chooses an arbitrary swap among swaps with the same best resulting     │
│                          │ maximum pack load, and accepts only strict makespan reductions. This misses zero-makespan │
│                          │ swaps that reduce load variance and can expose a better makespan-reducing swap in a later │
│                          │ iteration.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Select, among all makespan-optimal candidate swaps, the one with the greatest reduction   │
│                          │ in the sum of squared pack loads. Such swaps preserve the primary maximum-load objective  │
│                          │ while improving overall GPU balance. They are accepted when they either strictly lower    │
│                          │ the maximum load or keep it unchanged while strictly reducing variance. The variance      │
│                          │ delta is computed algebraically from only the source and destination loads, so it does    │
│                          │ not require materializing all pack loads per candidate.                                   │
