│ patch_description        │ Replace the per-redundant-expert Python greedy loop with batched discrete water-filling.  │
│                          │ For a logical expert with load `w`, its successive replica candidates have priorities `w  │
│                          │ / 2`, `w / 3`, and so on; selecting the highest `num_redundant` priorities gives the same │
│                          │ minimax replica allocation as repeatedly assigning the next replica to the current        │
│                          │ highest-loaded expert.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The candidate rank is initially bounded near the average number of extra copies per       │
│                          │ logical expert. It doubles only when the selected top-k boundary could still be affected  │
│                          │ by an omitted candidate. This substantially reduces tensor allocation and top-k work for  │
│                          │ normal load distributions, while retaining exact allocation for highly skewed cases by    │
│                          │ expanding up to the required rank. The implementation also handles zero-load experts with │
│                          │ ordered negative tie-break priorities so selected replica ranks remain contiguous.        │
